8. Changed condition: Up Next queue
The application introduces an Up Next queue where songs are frequently added at both ends and removed from the front.

Music Player + Queue - Concept by Tanmay Saxena on Dribbble
 
Under this changed condition, ArrayDeque becomes the better choice.

Example:


java
import java.util.ArrayDeque;

public class UpNextQueue {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        ArrayDeque<String> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();

        // Add songs at both ends
        queue.addFirst("Song A");
        queue.addLast("Song B");
        queue.addLast("Song C");

        // Remove the next song
        String nextSong = queue.removeFirst();

        System.out.println("Now Playing: " + nextSong);
        System.out.println("Up Next: " + queue);
    }
}
