9. Alternative concept: Plain array with manual shifting
If the playlist were stored in a normal fixed-size array, insertion and removal would require manually shifting elements.

Example:


java
class SongPlaylist {

    String[] songs;
    int size;

    SongPlaylist(int capacity) {
        songs = new String[capacity];
        size = 0;
    }

    // Add at the end
    void add(String song) {
        if (size < songs.length) {
            songs[size++] = song;
        }
    }

    // Insert at a given position
    void insert(int index, String song) {

        if (index < 0 || index > size ||
                size == songs.length) {
            return;
        }

        for (int i = size; i > index; i--) {
            songs[i] = songs[i - 1];
        }

        songs[index] = song;
        size++;
    }

    // Remove from a given position
    void remove(int index) {

        if (index < 0 || index >= size) {
            return;
        }

        for (int i = index; i < size - 1; i++) {
            songs[i] = songs[i + 1];
        }
        songs[--size] = null;
    }
    // Access k-th song
    String get(int k) {
        if (k < 0 || k >= size)
            return null;
        return songs[k];
    }
}
